      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at RMU | Robert Morris University Skip to main content Top Header - Left Students Faculty / Staff Careers Top Header - Right Request Info Visit Make a Gift APPLY NOW Search the RMU Website You must have JavaScript enabled to use this form. Search Main navigation Why Choose RMU? WHY CHOOSE RMU? Reputation and Outcomes RMU is Affordable Campus Experience Thriving City Personal Attention Flexible Learning Athletic Tradition Admissions ADMISSIONS Freshman Admissions Graduate & Doctoral Admissions Transfer Admissions International Admissions Part-time, Readmission and Guest Students Veterans & Military Families Student Financial Services Financial Aid Office College Affordability Academy Academics ACADEMICS Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Doctoral Programs Certificate Programs Online Programs Schools & Departments Office of the Provost Special Academic Programs Research & Grants Administration Academic Calendar Elaine Boyd Library Alumni & Giving ALUMNI & GIVING Alumni Association Alumni Events Giving Options Update Your Information Athletics ATHLETICS RMUColonials.com UPMC Events Center Island Sports Center Club Sports Historic Highlights Support Colonials About RMU ABOUT RMU Office of the President Board of Trustees Mission, Vision, and Values University History Newsroom Corporate Partnerships Events RMU Center for Veterans and Military Families Public Safety Bayer Center for Nonprofit Management Academic Media Center Covestro Center for Community Engagement Menu GIVE | VISIT | GET INFO | APPLY Careers at RMU Applicant Login Sign Up for Job Alerts Clear Search Results Search Jobs Job Search Search Filters WORK TYPE Faculty Full-Time 5 Faculty Part-Time 14 Staff Full-Time 27 Staff Part-Time 24 Student Worker 10 LOCATIONS Island Sports Center 12 Moon Campus 68 CATEGORIES Administrative Support/Clerical 1 Athletics 21 College of Business and STEM 9 College of Health Sciences 15 Dean of Students 2 Enrollment Management 2 Facilities 2 Financial Operations 2 Institutional Advancement 1 International Visiting Scholar 1 Marketing & Public Relations 2 Other 16 Public Safety/Police 3 Student Experience 4 SEARCH RESULTS POSITION DEPARTMENT LOCATION Athletic Ticket Sales and Service Account Representative Athletics Administration Moon Campus RMU Athletics Ticket Sales and Service Account Representative position will learn and expand his/her knowledge of the fundamentals of the sales process through group sales, new season ticket sales and renewals across all ticketed sports. The Account Representative position will receive training, development and be provided the opportunity for rapid career advancement to Senior level sales roles, and leadership positions with added responsibility. Athletic Trainer Athletics Training Moon Campus Serves as athletic trainer for the intercollegiate varsity program within the guidelines, rules and regulations of Robert Morris University and the NCAA. Administrative Coordinator Bayer Center for Nonprofit Management (BCNM) and the Covestro Center for Community Engagement (CCEC) Bayer Center for Nonprofit Management and Covestro Center for Community Engagement Moon Campus The Administrative Coordinator provides comprehensive administrative and operational support to the Bayer Center for Nonprofit Management (BCNM) and the Covestro Center for Community Engagement (CCCE). This role requires exceptional organizational skills, technology skills, attention to detail, proactive problem-solving abilities, and the capacity to manage diverse tasks efficiently in a fast-paced environment. The Administrative Assistant will serve as a key point of contact, manage schedules and communications, and support the smooth functioning of both Centers activities and programs. Administrative Coordinator:  Collaborative Learning Institute (CLI) Collaborative Learning Institute Moon Campus The Administrative Coordinator provides comprehensive administrative and operational support for the Collaborative Learning Institute (CLI). This position serves as a primary point of contact for students, visitors, faculty, staff, employers, vendors, and community partners while helping to ensure that CLI’s daily operations, facilities, events, contracts, invoicing, and administrative processes are organized and running smoothly. The Administrative Coordinator maintains a welcoming and professional environment for students and visitors and works closely with CLI Leadership and university departments to coordinate the logistical and administrative needs of the Institute. The position requires strong organization, attention to detail, follow-through, customer service, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced learning and event environment. Assistant Director, Strategic Communications Athletics Media Relations Moon Campus The Assistant Director, Strategic Communications assists with the creation and implementation of overall design strategy across all aspects of the athletic department and is responsible for oversight of all media relations functions for assigned sports, within the guidelines, rules, and regulations of the University and NCAA. Assistant Coach, Men’s D4 Club Ice Hockey Campus Recreation Island Sports Center The Assistant Coach, Men’s D4 Club Ice Hockey is a part-time position not eligible for University benefits. Work hours are limited to 950 per calendar year and less than 29 hours per week on a regular basis.\n\nThe University is a proud member of the ACHA with successful hockey programs at the Men’s D1 and D3 levels.\n\nThe team practices 2-3 times per week and plays games most weekends during the season. \n\t\nThere are 3-5 travel weekends during the season which include Fridays. Preference is for the coach to attend all practices and games. Director of Student Accessibility Center For Student Success Moon Campus The Director of Student Accessibility provides equal opportunity to students with disabilities to ensure equal access to education programs, services, and benefits, and to promote a welcoming campus environment for students requiring accommodations. The Director advocates for students with disabilities and seeks to empower them to become their own and best advocates. The Director provides technical assistance and guidance to faculty about providing accommodations to students. The position also provides personal counseling, education, professional programming, as well as services and resources for students with disabilities to create inclusive learning environments. Serving as the main disability representative and voice on campus, this staff member's primary focus will be the education of students, parents, faculty, and staff centered around standards, practices, letters of accommodations, and appropriate services provided through programs, workshops, and personal meetings. This role operates with a post-secondary disabililty framework and accommodation determinations are made through an individualized, interactive process. The Director will also provide academic advisement and support to a designated group of undergraduate students. Media Project Manager Academic Media Center Moon Campus Robert Morris University’s Academic Media Center (AMC) seeks a highly organized and skilled individual to serve as Media Project Manager. This role is central to the operational efficiency and cross-campus coordination of the university’s media ecosystem, ensuring that the AMC's resources are effectively deployed to support academic, athletic, branding, and student experience initiatives. The Media Project Manager is responsible for administering the center's assignment system, facilitating seamless collaboration with key campus stakeholders, managing the booking of physical resources, and convening student content producers. This role includes direct student mentorship to support experiential learning in media production and project management. This is a Part-time, non-benefit eligible position limited to no more than 950 hours in a calendar year. Digital Media Content Creator Brand Department Moon Campus We are seeking a creative and driven Part-Time Digital Media Content Creator to join our team. This role is a perfect fit for a recent graduate who is passionate about storytelling and visual media. You will play a key role in capturing the vibrant life of our campus, highlighting our schools and programs, and bringing campus stories to life through high-quality photography and videography. This position offers flexible part-time hours, allowing you to build your portfolio while continuing to collaborate with a team that already values your work and vision. Men’s Hockey Operations Coordinator Men's Ice Hockey Moon Campus Responsible for the management of all equipment and apparel purchases and game set-up for the men’s hockey program. Works with vendors, coaches and students. Maintains athletic equipment, including repair and upkeep within the guidelines, rules and regulations of Robert Morris University and the NCAA. This position requires responsibilities with team travel which may include hotel, buses, airplane and team meal reservations. This position may also include duties with video editing and video editing systems. Duties will be expanded as required and will be adjusted based on incumbent’s strengths and weaknesses. Academic Advisor and Retention Specialist Center For Student Success Moon Campus The Academic Advisor and Retention Specialist position at Robert Morris University is a team member within the Center for Student Success. As a member of the Center for Student Success Team, this student-centered position supports undergraduate recruitment and retention initiatives across programs in the assigned areas. Primary responsibilities include academic advising, participating in recruitment initiatives and activities, providing oversight to several key technology based retention strategies, and serving as a point of contact for undergraduates with specific departments and programs. Work is performed under the supervision of the Director of the Center for Student Success and includes collaboration with Academic Department Heads and/or other program personnel. Assistant Coach, Women's Soccer, Part-Time Women's Soccer Moon Campus RMU Athletics is looking for a Part-Time Women’s Soccer Coach that will assist the Head Coach in the overall management, competitive advancement, and daily operations of the collegiate soccer program.  This is a part-time, not benefit eligible position limited to 950 hours in a calendar year and generally no more than 29 hours on a weekly basis. Assistant Coach, Men's Soccer, Part-Time Men's Soccer Moon Campus The Part-Time Assistant Men’s Soccer Coach will assist the Head Coach and full-time staff with the overall operation of the men’s soccer program. This position will support the daily preparation, development, and management of student-athletes while helping promote a positive, competitive, and team-first environment.  This is a non-benefit eligible position limited to 950 hours per calendar year and generally no more than 29 hours a week on a regular basis. Assistant Coach, Softball, Part-Time Softball Moon Campus This individual plays a pivotal role in the strategic development, competitive success, and holistic growth of the student-athletes within the program. Operating in a high-stakes, fast-paced NCAA Division I environment, this position supports the Head Coach in all aspects of program management, including technical skill instruction (such as hitting, pitching, or defensive specialist work), tactical game-planning, and the identification and recruitment of elite-level prospects. Beyond the field and batting cages, the Assistant Coach serves as a dedicated mentor committed to fostering academic integrity, personal accountability, and strict compliance with all NCAA, conference, and university regulations, ultimately helping to build a championship-caliber culture that elevates the institution's athletic profile. Assistant Coach, Women's Volleyball, Part-Time Women's Volleyball Moon Campus RMU Athletics is looking for a Part-Time Women’s Volleyball Coach will support the Head Coach in the overall management, competitive advancement, and daily operations of the collegiate volleyball program.  This is a part-time not benefit eligible position limited to 950 hours in a calendar year and generally no more than 29 hours a week on a regular basis. Assistant Coach, Football, Part-Time Football Moon Campus RMU Athletics is looking for a Part-Time Assistant Football Coach.  This is a part-time not benefit eligible position limited to 950 hours in a calendar year and generally no more than 29 hours per week on a regular basis. Director of Ticket Operations – Athletics and UPMC Events Center UPMC Events Center Moon Campus The Director of Ticket Operations is a dual-purpose leadership role managing all ticketing mechanics, inventory control, and box office logistics for Robert Morris University’s five NCAA Division I ticketed sports (Football, Men's Basketball, Women's Basketball, Men's Hockey, and Women's Hockey) alongside third-party entertainment hosted at the UPMC Events Center. This position serves as the technical architect behind the ticketing software, acting as the primary financial liaison for national concert promoters, the RMU Athletic Business Office, and the RMU Student-Athlete Compliance Office. Operations Associate Operations, ISC Island Sports Center This position is located at the RMU Island Sports Center (ISC).  This duties of the position require manual labor and semi-skilled work in the care of the ISC.  This position is considered essential and is required to report to work as scheduled during University closings. Public Safety Officer, ISC University Police Island Sports Center This position is responsible for providing public safety and information services to the University community and Island Sports Center community, including all personnel and visitors.  It is a non-sworn, armed position reporting to the Director of Public Safety, Lieutenant, Sergeant. Head Coach, Women's Club Rugby Campus Recreation Moon Campus Robert Morris University is looking for a Head Coach for their Women's Rugby Team. The University is a proud member of the National Small College Rugby Organization (NSCRO) with successful men's and women's programs. The team practices 2-3 times per week and plays games most weekends during the season. There are 3-5 away games during the season which typically occur on weekends. Preference is for the coach to attend all practices and games.  This is a part-time, non benefit eligible role limited to working no more than 950 hours per calendar year. More Jobs 60 POSITION DEPARTMENT LOCATION Athletic Ticket Sales and Service Account Representative Athletics Administration Moon Campus RMU Athletics Ticket Sales and Service Account Representative position will learn and expand his/her knowledge of the fundamentals of the sales process through group sales, new season ticket sales and renewals across all ticketed sports. The Account Representative position will receive training, development and be provided the opportunity for rapid career advancement to Senior level sales roles, and leadership positions with added responsibility. Athletic Trainer Athletics Training Moon Campus Serves as athletic trainer for the intercollegiate varsity program within the guidelines, rules and regulations of Robert Morris University and the NCAA. Administrative Coordinator Bayer Center for Nonprofit Management (BCNM) and the Covestro Center for Community Engagement (CCEC) Bayer Center for Nonprofit Management and Covestro Center for Community Engagement Moon Campus The Administrative Coordinator provides comprehensive administrative and operational support to the Bayer Center for Nonprofit Management (BCNM) and the Covestro Center for Community Engagement (CCCE). This role requires exceptional organiza