ial Operations 0 Institutional Advancement 0 International Visiting Scholar 0 Marketing & Public Relations 0 Other 0 Public Safety/Police 0 Student Experience 0 SEARCH RESULTS POSITION DEPARTMENT LOCATION Adjunct Faculty Science - Meteorology (Part-Time) Science Moon Campus Adjunct (Part-time) faculty to teach undergraduate Meteorology and Earth Science courses including labs. Potential courses include Introduction to Meteorology lecture and lab, Climatology, Introduction to Geology and Lab, Hydrogeology. Part-Time Faculty - Sociology Social Sciences Moon Campus The position requires teaching undergraduate courses, such as Principles of Sociology, Social Problems, Marriage and Families, Race and Ethnicities, Women in Society and Deviant Behavior. Part-time Faculty - Psychology Psychology and Health Sciences Moon Campus Part-time faculty to teach one or more of the following on-ground undergraduate courses during Fall 2026 semester: PSYC1010 General Psychology (MWF 8-8:50am), PSYC1010 General Psychology (MWF 3-3:50am), PSYC3810 Industrial Psychology (MWF 9-9:50am). Part-Time Faculty-Cyber Investigations & Intelligence Computer and Information Systems Moon Campus This position requires the part-time faculty member to teach one or more graduate courses in the M.S. in Cyber Investigations and Intelligence program, housed in the Department of Computer and Information Systems within the School of Data Intelligence and Technology. Courses are taught on ground in a dedicated, non-attributed cyber lab on the Moon Campus and are aligned with the candidate's professional experience and academic preparation. Eligible courses include: CYBR 6120 Linux for Investigators; CYBR 6130 OSINT Collection, Analysis and Investigation; CYBR 6140 Offensive Cyber I; CYBR 6150 Programming for Investigators; CYBR 6230 Cyber Tradecraft; CYBR 6240 Offensive Cyber II; and CYBR 6800 Deep/Dark Web Investigations. Part-Time Faculty-Computer and Information Systems Computer and Information Systems Moon Campus Part-Time Faculty to teach courses offered by the Computer and Information Systems Department. More Jobs 4 POSITION DEPARTMENT LOCATION Adjunct Faculty Science - Meteorology (Part-Time) Science Moon Campus Adjunct (Part-time) faculty to teach undergraduate Meteorology and Earth Science courses including labs. Potential courses include Introduction to Meteorology lecture and lab, Climatology, Introduction to Geology and Lab, Hydrogeology. Part-Time Faculty - Sociology Social Sciences Moon Campus The position requires teaching undergraduate courses, such as Principles of Sociology, Social Problems, Marriage and Families, Race and Ethnicities, Women in Society and Deviant Behavior. Part-time Faculty - Psychology Psychology and Health Sciences Moon Campus Part-time faculty to teach one or more of the following on-ground undergraduate courses during Fall 2026 semester: PSYC1010 General Psychology (MWF 8-8:50am), PSYC1010 General Psychology (MWF 3-3:50am), PSYC3810 Industrial Psychology (MWF 9-9:50am). Part-Time Faculty-Cyber Investigations & Intelligence Computer and Information Systems Moon Campus This position requires the part-time faculty member to teach one or more graduate courses in the M.S. in Cyber Investigations and Intelligence program, housed in the Department of Computer and Information Systems within the School of Data Intelligence and Technology. Courses are taught on ground in a dedicated, non-attributed cyber lab on the Moon Campus and are aligned with the candidate's professional experience and academic preparation. Eligible courses include: CYBR 6120 Linux for Investigators; CYBR 6130 OSINT Collection, Analysis and Investigation; CYBR 6140 Offensive Cyber I; CYBR 6150 Programming for Investigators; CYBR 6230 Cyber Tradecraft; CYBR 6240 Offensive Cyber II; and CYBR 6800 Deep/Dark Web Investigations. Part-Time Faculty-Computer and Information Systems Computer and Information Systems Moon Campus Part-Time Faculty to teach courses offered by the C